;
; Can the guest read what the chipset drew?
;
; Bellatrix publishes each finished Denise frame at $01000000 with a
; descriptor at $01200000 (src/amiga/frame.h). Everything up to that point is
; verified on the Bellatrix side, by the census in src/amiga/bus.c. This is the
; other half, and it is the half that matters: the m68k reading the same frame
; back through the machine map.
;
; The two censuses are meant to be compared. Same background, same non-black
; count, same checksum means the frame the chipset composed is the frame the
; guest can see. Different means the bridge, not the chipset.
;
; NOWINDOW because this runs from the Startup-Sequence with nothing to display
; on yet, and because the claim being tested is readability, not presentation.
;
Echo >DEBUG: "[denise-view] --- reading the frame aperture"
DeniseView >DEBUG: NOWINDOW
Echo >DEBUG: "[denise-view] --- done"
